# keep CRLF exactly as stored, raw.githubusercontent.com serves the blob as-is
*.cmd -text

# Line endings by what runs the file, not by what the machine checking it out prefers.
# cmd.exe is the reason: a .bat with bare newlines can run its lines together around labels and
# goto, and the failure looks like a script bug rather than an encoding one. install.sh has the
# mirror of that problem, being piped straight into bash from a raw url, where a CR would come
# through as part of every line.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf

# The jar the wrapper scripts run, committed so a clone is usable without a build
*.jar binary
